      "side": 1,
      "message": "On old versions of Windows, the D3D12.dll in System32 will not have a D3D12GetInterface function exported because it doesn\u0027t exist. Even when DAWN_USE_AGILITY_SDK is defined, we want avoid crashing here. \n\nPrefer to re-structure as follows: \n```\nMaybeError PlatformFunctions::LoadD3D12() {\n  ...\n  std::string error;\n  if (mD3D12Lib.OpenSystemLibrary(L\"d3d12.dll\", \u0026error)) {\n    bool useAgilitySDK \u003d false;\n#ifdef DAWN_USE_AGILITY_SDK\n    useAgilitySDK \u003d mD3D12Lib.GetProc(..., \"D3D12GetInterface\", ...);\n#endif    \n    if (!useAgilitySDK) {\n      // Load all of the function pointers from D3D12.dll\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThen, functions like `CreateDevice`, `SerializeVersionedRootSignature` and `CreateVersionedRootSignatureDeserializer` can be like the following.\n\n```\nHRESULT PlatformFunctions::CreateDevice(...) {\n#ifdef DAWN_USE_AGILITY_SDK\n  if(mDeviceConfiguration) {\n    return mDeviceConfiguration-\u003eCreateDevice(...);\n  }\n#endif  \n  return d3d12CreateDevice(...);\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "4262ce80c613876fca2c235f190e84ada38c084f",
